  "claims": [
    "Typed substitution templates count and replace every occurrence of a chosen pure Wire argument by one actual contextual Step. The replacement proof track has exactly as many rewrite edges as template holes.",
    "Sixteen explicit Variation forms cover the wire-argument positions of the eighteen first-level cartesian equations, including two-to-one eta contraction, one-to-zero erased arguments, and one-to-two fork-composition duplication. Primitive fixed-gate and shape-unification overlaps are not included in this coverage claim.",
    "argumentAt reconstructs the original root by heterogeneous equality for every declared argument index. argumentAt_tag independently checks that its Variation tag equals the expected position tag; argument_coverage retains this tag check in the witness.",
    "The higher presentation explicitly supplies sixteen argument-naturality diagram families and two sequence/tensor separated-exchange families, with four pure context placements. Each generator boundary contains at most three actual rewrite Steps, including under arbitrary repeated pure placements.",
    "Pure Homotopy.whisker maps existing generators and proof-groupoid laws to contexts and preserves Four-constructor count. No fixed whole-normalizer or arbitrary parallel-path comparison is a higher generator.",
    "discardTrack derives a comparison for any inner proof track followed by the discardAfter equation, by recursion on that track and only the one-step discard argument diagram plus proof-groupoid laws.",
    "discardedParallel constructs a higher comparison of ANY two parallel inner proof tracks AFTER postcomposition with a discard wire. This does not establish comparison of the original tracks before that context.",
    "The constructed discardedParallel witness uses exactly stepCount(first)+stepCount(second) local higher generators. Its Four-constructor count is at most 23+12*(trackConstructorCount(first)+trackConstructorCount(second)). No other proof paths are enumerated by the construction.",
    "The counting metrics exclude Step/Wire/context/boundary payloads and shared libraries; input trackConstructorCount includes refl, step, comp and inverse nodes, while stepCount counts only actual rewrite edges.",
    "Pure local higher generators and cells embed into the standalone mixed cartesian-wiring catalogue. Embedded cells have empty guard support; a mixed placement adds exactly its fixed-context needs. Updated joint-kernel repair retains arbitrary correlated prior data and original input.",
    "The discard-context constructor bound transfers to mixed placements. Actual full-state MAC contexts are instantiated, including a frame retaining the MAC result on the left while only the pure right branch is discarded. Its support is exactly {stage}."
  ],
