  "limits": [
    "Wire-argument coverage is not exhaustive critical-overlap classification. Root/root and fixed structural-gate overlaps, alternative update schedules and a complete finite higher basis for all pure tracks remain to be connected or proved.",
    "The chosen higher presentation is explicit and local. Theorems are relative to these supplied diagram families. No global cartesian higher coherence, unrestricted directed termination or complete cryptographic/mixed union is established.",
    "The previous eighteen first-level equations and the eighteen new higher families are distinct sets. Families allow typed substitution and context; the number of all ground instances is not finite.",
    "discardedParallel compares tracks in a post-discard context only. Formal cancellation removes a rewrite-proof suffix, not a wire operation or a stochastic continuation. It does not recover pre-discard observations or prove coherence of the original inner tracks.",
    "Application to an original game requires that the relevant pure branch is already discarded, with required observations retained elsewhere. Adding discard to forget the target observations is not a proof of the original full-state game guarantee.",
    "The linear counts are counts of local generators and Four syntax constructors for this constructed witness, not total certificate bytes, minimal proofs, checking time, native runtime or an equal-information ordinary-proof lower bound. A supplied local cell may yield a smaller comparison than the generic discard construction.",
    "Only deterministic pure Wire arguments may be duplicated or erased. These rules do not justify copying probabilistic boxes or removing their physical costs. The generic joint repair theorem uses one mixed placement; repeated placement supports are separately tracked.",
    "The mixed catalogue here is the pure structural one from the preceding step, not a completed merge of all MAC/fusion rules. Existing MAC kernels, state/trace and indexed security conditions are unchanged; no new security bound or continuing native-machine contract is proved.",
    "No new independent ordinary baseline, total-cost experiment or primary-source priority review is provided."
  ],
  "novelty": {
    "status": "unconfirmed",
    "finding": "Bounded local higher diagrams now handle nonlinear wire arguments, and a constructive discard-context coherence theorem with linear Four-constructor bounds is derived without a whole-normalization generator. This is a concrete restricted theorem within the research foundation, not a claim of novelty for naturality, terminality or groupoid contraction principles.",
    "next_evidence": "Classify and fill remaining fixed-gate/root critical overlaps, establish the complete pure and mixed higher basis, retain full observation/resource/native contracts, compare ordinary methods with identical information and sharing, and review primary results for the proposed observation-relative proof-construction method."
  },
